WEBVTT

00:00:00.628 --> 00:00:03.250
The Newspaper Chase.

00:00:03.310 --> 00:00:08.654
The time is one o'clock in the morning.

00:00:08.714 --> 00:00:14.838
The place is the Ritesville town art gallery.

00:00:14.898 --> 00:00:19.622
A window opens and a man comes in.

00:00:19.682 --> 00:00:25.716
His name is Harry Black, and he is a thief.

00:00:25.776 --> 00:00:31.382
It is dark in the art gallery, but Harry has a light.

00:00:31.442 --> 00:00:35.393
He looks across the room at a painting.

00:00:35.453 --> 00:00:39.204
"There it is!" he says.

00:00:39.264 --> 00:00:42.885
Harry moves quickly across the room.

00:00:42.945 --> 00:00:46.156
He stands and looks at the painting.

00:00:46.216 --> 00:00:50.446
"A million dollars for this?" he thinks.

00:00:50.506 --> 00:00:53.032
"I don't understand it."

00:00:53.092 --> 00:00:56.848
But he takes a knife from his coat.

00:00:56.908 --> 00:01:04.402
Then he takes the painting very, very slowly from its frame.

00:01:04.463 --> 00:01:11.716
Harry goes back across the room to the window, but he walks into a table.

00:01:11.776 --> 00:01:16.978
There is a beautiful blue glass vase on the table.

00:01:17.038 --> 00:01:22.440
It falls on the floor and breaks into a hundred pieces.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:24.948
Harry smiles.

00:01:25.008 --> 00:01:29.390
"Is that a million-dollar vase?" he thinks.
 
00:01:29.450 --> 00:01:31.991
"It isn't now!"

00:01:32.051 --> 00:01:36.982
He runs across the pieces of glass to the window.

00:01:37.042 --> 00:01:42.074
Harry has a room in Mrs. Allen's rooming house.

00:01:42.134 --> 00:01:47.676
He goes quietly up to his room and closes the door.

00:01:47.736 --> 00:01:52.694
Mrs. Allen and her daughter, Janey, are sleeping.

00:01:52.754 --> 00:01:55.452
They don't hear him.

00:01:55.512 --> 00:02:00.634
In his room, Harry takes the painting from his bag.

00:02:00.694 --> 00:02:07.108
He puts it in a newspaper, then he puts the newspaper under his bed.

00:02:07.167 --> 00:02:11.380
In the morning, Janey Allen is in the kitchen.

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:15.263
She's putting old bottles into a box.

00:02:15.322 --> 00:02:20.341
"Recycling is important," Janey thinks.

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:26.140
On the TV, a reporter is at the Ritesville art gallery.

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:29.232
He is talking about the painting.

00:02:29.292 --> 00:02:33.816
"It's a million-dollar painting," he is saying.

00:02:33.876 --> 00:02:36.738
"Here's a photo of it."

00:02:36.798 --> 00:02:42.072
Now the reporter is talking about the blue glass vase.

00:02:42.132 --> 00:02:47.146
"It's in a hundred pieces now," he says.

00:02:47.206 --> 00:02:50.682
Janey looks at the photo of the vase.

00:02:50.742 --> 00:02:53.448
Then she asks her mother,

00:02:53.508 --> 00:02:57.090
"Do you have any old bottles?"

00:02:57.150 --> 00:03:00.761
"No," Mrs. Allen says.

00:03:00.821 --> 00:03:02.922
"That's all, Janey.

00:03:02.982 --> 00:03:07.234
But the newspaper recycling truck is coming today."

00:03:07.294 --> 00:03:10.866
"Of course!" Janey says.

00:03:10.926 --> 00:03:13.428
"It's Friday!"

00:03:13.488 --> 00:03:16.860
Harry isn't in his room.

00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:21.631
He is talking on his telephone to a man in Seattle.

00:03:21.691 --> 00:03:29.523
The man wants the painting, but Harry isn't happy.

00:03:29.583 --> 00:03:32.934
"Five thousand dollars?" Harry says.

00:03:32.994 --> 00:03:38.216
"No! It's a million-dollar painting!

00:03:38.276 --> 00:03:40.356
What?

00:03:40.416 --> 00:03:46.920
No, I want fifty thousand, not five!

00:03:46.980 --> 00:03:49.281
What?

00:03:49.340 --> 00:03:57.220
The painting? Yes, I have it, and it's OK."
 
00:03:57.280 --> 00:04:01.884
Janey is looking for old newspapers.

00:04:01.944 --> 00:04:07.618
Early on Friday mornings, she takes them from every room in the house.

00:04:07.678 --> 00:04:13.253
Then later, the newspaper recycling truck arrives.

00:04:13.313 --> 00:04:18.644
Janey opens Harry's door and looks into his room.

00:04:18.703 --> 00:04:24.441
She always takes his old newspapers or bottles for recycling.

00:04:24.501 --> 00:04:26.852
"Ah!" she thinks.

00:04:26.912 --> 00:04:30.853
"There's a newspaper under Harry's bed."

00:04:30.913 --> 00:04:36.714
Janey puts the old newspapers into a black recycling box.

00:04:36.774 --> 00:04:41.096
She runs from the house and sees the truck.

00:04:41.156 --> 00:04:47.823
"Wait!" she says. And she quickly gives the box to one of the men.

00:04:47.882 --> 00:04:52.190
Harry is coming back to the house.

00:04:52.250 --> 00:04:57.484
He sees the recycling truck, and he sees Janey.

00:04:57.544 --> 00:05:01.196
"It's Friday!" he says.

00:05:01.256 --> 00:05:06.068
"The newspaper! Oh, no!"
  
00:05:06.128 --> 00:05:09.600
Harry chases after the truck.

00:05:09.660 --> 00:05:14.494
"Wait! Wait!" he says.
 
00:05:14.554 --> 00:05:17.191
Janey watches him.

00:05:17.251 --> 00:05:22.310
"What is he doing?" she thinks.
  
00:05:22.370 --> 00:05:26.313
Harry jumps into the back of the truck.

00:05:26.373 --> 00:05:30.186
"I want my newspaper!" he says.

00:05:30.246 --> 00:05:33.558
"Where's my newspaper?"

00:05:33.618 --> 00:05:38.442
But there are thousands of newspapers in the truck.

00:05:38.502 --> 00:05:42.775
Janey walks quickly from the house to the truck.

00:05:42.834 --> 00:05:48.050
"Why is your newspaper important, Harry?" she asks. 

00:05:48.200 --> 00:05:51.294
"It's two days old."

00:05:51.354 --> 00:05:54.045
But Harry doesn't hear her.

00:05:54.105 --> 00:06:00.328
He is thinking, "My million-dollar painting! Where is it?"

00:06:00.388 --> 00:06:05.119
The men from the recycling truck are watching Harry, too.

00:06:05.179 --> 00:06:09.580
But now Janey is looking at Harry's shoe.

00:06:09.640 --> 00:06:15.652
"There's some blue glass in Harry's shoe," Janey thinks.

00:06:15.712 --> 00:06:20.402
"Where? Oh!"
 
00:06:20.462 --> 00:06:27.074
Suddenly, she remembers the photo of the blue glass vase on the TV.

00:06:27.133 --> 00:06:31.814
She looks again at the piece of glass in Harry's shoe.

00:06:31.874 --> 00:06:36.646
"Is it from the vase in the art gallery?" she thinks.
 
00:06:36.706 --> 00:06:40.126
"Is Harry Black the thief?"

00:06:40.186 --> 00:06:44.498
The men from the recycling truck are angry.

00:06:44.558 --> 00:06:46.514
"We're going now,"

00:06:46.574 --> 00:06:49.671
they are saying. "We're late."

00:06:49.731 --> 00:06:54.303
"But I want my newspaper!" Harry says.

00:06:54.363 --> 00:06:59.050
In the house, Janey is talking to the police on the telephone.

00:06:59.200 --> 00:07:03.026
"Maybe I'm wrong," she is saying.

00:07:03.086 --> 00:07:06.728
"But there's blue glass in his shoe ...

00:07:06.787 --> 00:07:08.308
What? ...

00:07:08.368 --> 00:07:13.100
Yes, he's looking for the newspaper now."

00:07:13.160 --> 00:07:17.020
Two policemen arrive quickly.

00:07:17.080 --> 00:07:21.390
"Let's look at your shoe," they say to Harry.
 
00:07:21.450 --> 00:07:24.300
Harry doesn't understand.

00:07:24.360 --> 00:07:27.712
"What's wrong?" he asks.
 
00:07:27.772 --> 00:07:32.004
One of the policemen takes the glass from Harry's shoe.

00:07:32.064 --> 00:07:36.300
"This is a very expensive piece of glass," he says. 

00:07:36.400 --> 00:07:41.368
"From a very expensive vase. Remember?"
 
00:07:41.428 --> 00:07:45.259
Suddenly, Harry understands.

00:07:45.319 --> 00:07:49.463
"Oh, no!" he says.
 
00:07:49.523 --> 00:07:53.286
Police cars and policemen arrive.

00:07:53.345 --> 00:07:58.129
The men look in the truck for the million-dollar painting.

00:07:58.189 --> 00:08:04.604
Later, they find the right newspaper—and they find the painting.

00:08:04.664 --> 00:08:09.086
"Good work, Janey," one of the policemen says.

00:08:09.146 --> 00:08:12.208
"And there's a reward."

00:08:12.268 --> 00:08:17.636
"Maybe I can buy a painting with the reward!" Janey says.

00:08:17.696 --> 00:08:19.893
"I like pictures!"